vaccinations are at the center of the  biden administration's strategy to end  the pandemic to that end the white house  made january 4 the deadline for larger  companies to get their workers  vaccinated or implement weekly testing  it could affect 84 million workers  nearly three-quarters of america's  workforce some republican governors have  already threatened to sue over the  measure ed o'keefe has been following  this for us at the white house ed good  morning good morning to you nate happy  friday the potential legal blowback is  mounting despite recent polling that  shows most americans support these kind  of mandates and the white house is  defending the new rule saying it's just  all about keeping american workers safe  as mandates continue to be a flash point  across the country the labor department  thursday announced it's implementing a  new vaccination rule requiring companies  with 100 or more employees to get their  workers fully vaccinated by january 4th  or test them for covet 19 at least once  a week fines for not complying could  reach nearly 14 thousand dollars per  worker per violation we know that  vaccines absolutely save lives  and we know that mandates work with  cases rising or holding steady in at  least 27 states the white house says the  mandate is about maximizing compliance  how confident is the white house these  will hold up in court with a lot of gop  states threatening legal action  so we're pretty we're pretty confident  the administration clearly has the  authority to protect workers on capitol  hill some senators said more mandates  are not the answer it's probably the  most frightening ultimatum  that businesses have had to contend with  it's essentially  an unfunded mandate kevin grigg is an  engineering and consulting firm ceo  based in connecticut i think it's going  to take months for  all of us  to figure out exactly how this is going  to work and during that period of time  at least  we're going to have a lot of sunken  costs  some other business leaders say they're  going to wait to see how this all plays  out in the courts but some of the  nation's biggest labor unions and  business groups like the u.s chamber of  commerce are endorsing the new mandates  and private companies are taking their  own steps the ford motor company for  example says all of its 32 000 u.s  workers have to be vaccinated by  december 8.  tony  all right ed thank you very much
 

